From 9cf1970627718316e1f34c11dd80ce1b63824666 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 17:41:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix the peer conflict that breaks npm install
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`npm install` fails outright on a clean checkout:

  peer vite@"^4.2.0 || ^5.0.0" from @vitejs/plugin-react@4.3.1
  Found: vite@7.3.1
  Conflicting peer dependency: vite@5.4.21

The project moved to Vite 7 while the React plugin stayed on 4.3.1, which
only claims support up to Vite 5. Anyone cloning the repo has to pass
--legacy-peer-deps to get anywhere, which quietly accepts a resolution npm
considers wrong.

@vitejs/plugin-react 5.2.0 declares support through Vite 7, so upgrading
it makes the tree resolve honestly. `npm install` now succeeds with no
flags.

`npm ci` was unaffected — it installs from the lockfile without
re-resolving peers — which is why deploys kept working and this only bit
people installing locally.

Verified after the upgrade: install resolves clean, typecheck passes,
build succeeds, 39 tests pass, and the landing page renders with its
fonts and logo intact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MakDNwh5UsmgrDJqXtziVu
---
 package.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
index b57517b..e0ded68 100644
--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
     "@eslint/js": "9.9.1",
     "@types/react": "18.3.5",
     "@types/react-dom": "18.3.0",
-    "@vitejs/plugin-react": "4.3.1",
+    "@vitejs/plugin-react": "^5.2.0",
     "@vitest/ui": "4.1.2",
     "autoprefixer": "10.4.18",
     "eslint": "9.39.4",
